From 8d476a9a7a5e7546f8b124133e9f3df57e8e0651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jasmine <jasmine@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0136: per-layer mixed-swap bounds; no fallback for a
 client swap; requeue

A mixed swap (backboardd's own layer 6 next to Maps' drawable, swap 618 in
logs/netlog-gate135.txt) was classified as a client swap by j0135, so every layer
in it took the 100 ms client rules.  backboardd's own layer sits behind Maps' GPU
work on the single ring; its ticket/gpuSeqno probe expired, rejectFrame(2) fell
back, and the display stayed synchronous for the rest of the boot (render tickets
suspended, every frame ungated).

j0136 classifies per layer:

- an own layer gets SWEET_FB_OWN_TICKET_MS (1000 ms) for ticket and gpuSeqno,
  whether it is alone or next to a client layer; only client layers skip the
  ticket wait (j0134) and keep the old 100 ms probe when that switch is off;
- queuePresent's admission is per layer too: a client layer never gates readiness,
  and an own layer with a ticket or gpuSeqno gets the 1000 ms tracked admission,
  never the 100 ms untracked one;
- a swap carrying a client layer never calls queueFallback, whatever the reason
  (ticket, gpuSeqno, present scope, queuePresent validity or a stuck latch).  It
  is dropped or completed by the j0133/j0134 client-layer paths and the queue
  stays active.  Own-only swaps keep j0132's fallback rules, including the
  stuck-presenter escape.

j0136 also re-enables queue mode after a fallback (boot-arg sweetfb_requeue=0
turns it off, default on) instead of staying synchronous for the boot.  Once 30
synchronous presents over at least 3 s were clean, no render ticket is live, no
latch or accepted frame is in flight, the newest begun swap has ended and
quarantined storage has finished its GPU work, queue mode is restored:
fQueueActive=1, fSwapWait=0, fEpoch++ (retires sync-interval swap tokens), the
clean streak reset and quarantine holds released.  Render-ticket epochs are
separate and unchanged, so the next BEGIN after sweet_ticket_query reports bit 3
gets a real generation again.  A SwapEnd for a swap begun before the requeue has
no queue token; it is completed as a stale transaction instead of spinning in the
token wait or faulting the re-enabled queue.  No build or boot has been done for
this patch.
